vasu: Quick headslip in sampleapp onboarding: when users enable @opentelemetry auto-instrument + REDACT_STRICT=1, logs show `req_id: -`. Incoming header X-Request-Id is present on the HTTP call. Repro with docker/scratch.

tara: Likely middleware ordering + redact. If OTEL runs before our request-id middleware it can capture context and our log hook never sees req.id.

lee: Short patch: make our log hook resilient to wrapped reqs and scrubbed headers. Fallback order: req.id, req.headers['x-request-id'], res.getHeader('x-request-id'), then try OTEL span attribute. Example:
```js
function resolveReqId(req,res){
  const maybe = (req && req.id) || (req && req.headers && req.headers['x-request-id']) || (res && res.getHeader && res.getHeader('x-request-id'));
  if(maybe) return maybe;
  try{
    const api = require('@opentelemetry/api');
    const span = api.trace.getSpan(api.context.active());
    return (span && span.attributes && (span.attributes['http.request_id'] || span.attributes['x-request-id'])) || '-';
  }catch(e){ return '-'; }
}
```

security: If we log raw request ids under REDACT_STRICT that's a privacy problem. Recommend two controls: REDACT_ALLOWLIST_HEADERS (default include x-request-id) and HASH_REQID=true to log stable HMAC(id) instead of raw value. Use KMS-backed key in prod.

lee: Agreed. We'll add a unit test simulating OTEL replacing req object and REDACT_STRICT zeroing headers. Hotfix: fallback resolve + support HASH_REQID env. Longer-term: update quickstart to show request-id middleware before auto-instrument.

vasu: I'll open a small PR with the hotfix + test + docs note. pinging security for review on hashing.

